  "question": {
    "text": "An astronaut whose height is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1.50</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>m</mtext></math> floats \"feet down\" in an orbiting space shuttle at a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>r</mtext><mo>=</mo><mroot><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>67</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mroot><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>m</mtext></math> away from the centre of Earth. The magnitude of difference between the gravitational acceleration at her feet and at her head is found to be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>N</mtext><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>. What is the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>?&nbsp; &nbsp;<br />\r[<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mtext>M</mtext><mtext>E</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>24</mn></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>kg</mtext></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>67</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi>kg</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>]"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "1.8",
  "solution": {
    "text": "The gravitational acceleration at any distance <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></math> from the center of Earth is&nbsp;<math><msub><mrow><mtext>a</mtext></mrow><mrow><mtext>g</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mtext>GM</mtext></mrow><mrow><mtext>E</mtext></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mtext>r</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></math>.<br />On differentiating, we get&nbsp;&nbsp;<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><msub><mrow><mtext>da</mtext></mrow><mrow><mtext>g</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mtext>GM</mtext></mrow><mrow><mtext>E</mtext></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mtext>r</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mtext>dr</mtext></math>,&nbsp;where <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><msub><mrow><mtext>da</mtext></mrow><mrow><mtext>g</mtext></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></math> is infinitesimal change in a due to differential change <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>dr</mi></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math>.<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><msub><mtext>da</mtext><mtext>g</mtext></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>6.67</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>24</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></mrow><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mroot><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>.67</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></mroot><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mn>1.50</mn></mfenced></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mtext>1.8</mtext><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mtext>&#8195;N</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn></math>"
  }
